    description: "Version 0.2"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NeoCortex0815/knowing-is-not-committing"
abstract: >-
  Independent replication and extension of MIT CSAIL's Sparks of Weight-Space
  Programming on Qwen3.5-0.8B. We rebuild the loop-reversal edit, add
  conditioned closing pushes and write a truth-gated reflex into 16 MLP
  neurons. A series of pre-registered tests asks how the model finds,
  recognises and commits to answers. Version 0.3 reports N30, the test
  pre-registered publicly in v0.2: a council of three answer-mode runs with
  our own thinking run as fallback solves 74 of 150 never-used MATH training
  problems, against 66 for answer mode alone and 67 for MIT's edit with
  thinking. It also reports N31: at the values the model writes while
  reasoning, its own tendency to stop does not track whether the value is
  correct (AUC 0.51), while a frozen linear probe does (0.68). Not
  peer-reviewed.
